    "problem_statement": "unregister_pickle_by_value function has inverted logic\n\nDescription\n\nThe `unregister_pickle_by_value` function appears to have inverted logic - it raises an error when a module IS a module type instead of when it's NOT a module type, and it adds modules to the registry instead of removing them.\n\nSteps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\nimport types\n\n# Create a dummy module\nimport sys\ndummy_module = types.ModuleType('dummy')\nsys.modules['dummy'] = dummy_module\n\n# Register it first\ncloudpickle.register_pickle_by_value(dummy_module)\n\n# Try to unregister - this should work but raises an error\ntry:\n    cloudpickle.unregister_pickle_by_value(dummy_module)\n    print(\"Unregistration successful\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n\n# Check if it's still in the registry (it shouldn't be)\nprint(f\"Still registered: {'dummy' in cloudpickle.list_registry_pickle_by_value()}\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior: The module should be unregistered without error.\nActual behavior: A ValueError is raised saying the module is already registered, and the module remains in the registry."
